 To solve this, we first find the value of $g(16)$.
\begin{align*} g(x) &= \sqrt{x}\\ g(16) &= \sqrt{16}\\ &=4 \end{align*}
Now, we can find the value of $t(g(16))$ using the value of $g(16)$.
\begin{align*} t(x) &= 3-g(x)\\ t(4) &= 3-\sqrt{4}\\ &= 3-2\\ &= 1 \end{align*}
